             <property name="whatsThis">
              <string>This value nominally scales the height for actors of this race and sex. In reality, it scales their entire size.</string>
             </property>
             <property name="alignment">
              <set>Qt::AlignRight|Qt::AlignTrailing|Qt::AlignVCenter</set>
             </property>
             <property name="value">
              <double>1.000000000000000</double>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item row="3" column="0">
            <widget class="QLabel" name="label_47">
             <property name="text">
              <string>Unused Body Tex.:</string>
             </property>
             <property name="buddy">
              <cstring>bodyTextureM</cstring>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item row="5" column="1" colspan="3">
            <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="voicetypeM">
             <property name="whatsThis">
              <string>Specify the default voicetype for male actors of this race. Male actors can only use male voicetypes. If you don't specify a voicetype, the hardcoded AdultMaleVoice1 form will be used.</string>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item row="1" column="1" colspan="3">
            <widget class="DKFormNIFPicker" name="skeletonM">
             <property name="whatsThis">
              <string>Specify an animation skeleton (*.nif) for actors of this race and sex.</string>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
           <item row="4" column="1" colspan="3">
            <widget class="DKFormPicker" name="decapArmorM">
             <property name="whatsThis">
              <string>When an actor is decapitated, the game will cut their skin mesh at the neck, based on vertex weights. If that were all the game did, however, then you'd see jagged edges following vertex boundaries, akin to cutting a piece of paper along a dotted zig-zagged line. Instead, the game will force the decapitated actor to equip a special Armor (often called a &quot;gore cap&quot;) that resembles two bloody stumps: one on the neck side and one on the head side. Here, you can specify that Armor, per sex.</string>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
          </layout>
         </widget>
        </widget>
       </item>
      </layout>
     </widget>
